        text: 'You want the MES terminal at line 4 (10.20.5.40, subnet 10.20.5.0/24) to fetch downtime data from the historian, a database that stores machine values with a timestamp, at 10.20.8.12.\n\nStep 1: same subnet? No: with /24 the first three numbers must match, and the third is 5 against 8. Step 2: so the traffic goes through the router or firewall. Step 3: IT must allow traffic from the terminal to the historian there. Step 4: put the name historian01.plant.local in the configuration, not the number, so the interface survives a server move.',
