        kind: 'worked',
        text: 'A new MES must read counter values from the historian every minute and fetch orders at night from the ERP (the business system for orders, stock and costs).\n\nStep 1: which systems, in which VLAN? MES server and historian in the production VLAN, ERP in the data-centre VLAN. Step 2: MES to historian stays inside one VLAN: no firewall rule needed. Step 3: MES to ERP goes through the firewall: one rule, from MES server to ERP server, port 443, that direction only. Step 4: request the rule with purpose and owner, and plan two weeks of lead time for it.',
